If I were ruler of the world, I'd:

- Ensure global governance to address climate change and global health challenges;

- Establish a progressive tax system where the wealthiest pay significantly more to build infrastructure for all;

- Implement a universal basic income to eradicate poverty;

- Pursue a sustainable agriculture model that promotes regenerative farming practices;

- Implement nationwide renewable energy targets;

- Establish global data privacy standards;

- Promote open-source technology development;

- Encourage free immigration policies to welcome people from around the world;

- Invest extensively in global education programs;

- Ensure fair representation in international bodies.

However, I'd avoid imposing my personal beliefs upon citizens and work toward consensus-based solutions that respect cultural diversity.

If I were ruler of the world, I would:

1) Draft a global constitution to establish standardized international laws and universal human rights;

2) Establish a multinational peacekeeping force with veto power over national military actions;

3) Implement taxation systems based on ability rather than geographical location or corporate status;

4) Create a world environmental regulatory agency with authority to enforce emission and conservation standards;

5) Establish a global digital identification system for all citizens worldwide;

6) Develop transparent, open-source technologies for all government departments;

7) Fund major global development projects focused on water rights, urban planning, and renewable energy;

8) Establish international humanitarian corridors and resettlement programs for refugees;

9) Create a global court system to hear international crimes against humanity cases;

10) Invest in sustainable agriculture and climate solutions that can provide food security for all nations.

For my historical gathering, I've invited:

- The great mathematicians Euclid and Descartes, who'll have fascinating discussions on geometry;
- Thomas Edison and Nikola Tesla for enlightening technological debates;
- Leonardo da Vinci and his impressive inventions;
- Winston Churchill and Mahatma Gandhi, who could provide insightful perspectives on history;
- Albert Einstein, the ultimate mind to impress with his physics explanations.

These figures offer diverse views on how history has evolved and make for compelling conversation topics. I can't wait to hear what they have to share!
